<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="133" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Adjustment report PDF</title>
    <phase>5 Firm feedback (WP5) — wave W5-2</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Generates a document from an existing projection and stores it through SpeFileStore; one new SpeFileStore method wraps a Graph call; content rules come from 130.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>OpenXml document assembly and a facade method addition with clear references; no AI and no auth model.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P5-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>130, 028</deps>
    <tags>bff, documents, spe</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Generate the firm adjustment report (FR-40, D-36) from 130's projection as a Word document, convert it to PDF through Microsoft Graph via SpeFileStore, store the PDF as a sprk_document linked from the submission (sprk_reportdocument), and expose a firm-scoped download route for the SPA — same content as the on-screen report, nothing internal.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in DocumentFormat.OpenXml, SharePoint Embedded through SpeFileStore (ADR-007) and Microsoft Graph drive item content.</role>

  <goal>AdjustmentReportService.GenerateAsync(subject) produces and stores the PDF idempotently; SpeFileStore gains one PDF-conversion method; GET external report route streams it to the right firm only; tests prove every projection item appears in the report and no internal field does.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-40 (acceptance: report lists every finding / adjustment shown on screen, nothing internal; attached to the email), D-36, FR-18 (PDF download on the SPA result screen), FR-16 / D-55 (E-Billing Output Files container, not indexed). 130 supplies the projection; 132 calls GenerateAsync before emailing; 134 calls the download route. Discovered: spec and plan call the PDF conversion "existing", but no BFF code calls Graph drive item content with format=pdf (grep "format=pdf" in src finds none; the path is described in projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/ws5-word-service-eval.md:30). DocumentFormat.OpenXml 3.5.1 is already referenced (Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj:217) — no new package. SpeFileStore facade: Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs:127 (DownloadFileAsync delegating to DriveItemOperations.cs:155). App-only access to the output container is allowed by 028 (D-67: Finance__EbillingOutputContainerId is in GraphModule.StampContainerSettingKeys). Document rows: sprk_documenttype is set as an OptionSetValue (example Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:517).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/AdjustmentReportService.cs (OpenXml builder, store, idempotency)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs and DriveItemOperations.cs (one method: download a drive item converted to PDF)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/AdjustmentReportEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs (one mount line; shared append point)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/AdjustmentReportServiceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/AdjustmentReportEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="130" status="pending">FirmFindingsProjection and the firm-scope check</dependency>
      <dependency task="028" status="pending">E-Billing Output Files container key and ownership</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Every SPE operation through SpeFileStore; the Graph conversion call lives in DriveItemOperations behind a SpeFileStore method; no GraphServiceClient outside Infrastructure/Graph.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-40, D-66">The report is rendered ONLY from 130's projection: the same items, citations and visibility rules as the screen; no Procedure Library link, no internal field.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Store the PDF in the E-Billing Output Files container (not indexed, 028) and link it from sprk_invoicesubmission.sprk_reportdocument (invoice outcomes: the invoice's originating submission). The intermediate .docx is deleted after conversion. If the container key is empty, fail with a stable ProblemDetails / job reason code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">GenerateAsync is idempotent: an existing report for the same outcome is reused; a changed outcome (for example Return after an earlier rejection report) creates a new document and repoints the link.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008, ADR-028, 040">Download route on the external group: CIAM caller checked with 130's firm-scope check; 404 with a stable code when no report exists; RequireEbillingEnabled().</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: no new package (OpenXml already referenced), publish-size delta recorded, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="076 review round 2 item 5 (notes/076-ruleset-endpoints.md section 8)">Clause text for firms comes only from RuleSetService.GetFirmClauseAsync(policyVersionId, invoiceFirmId, ct). invoiceFirmId is the firm of the INVOICE the finding belongs to: the invoice's sprk_vendororg, read server-side, and passed only after the route's own firm-membership check has established that the caller may see that invoice. Never pass a value from the request (body, query or route) and never the SPA identity's firm: a CIAM caller may belong to several firms, and internal callers have no SPA identity. Guid.Empty (the invoice has no firm) returns no text. Required test: a caller in two firms, viewing firm A's invoice, gets A's clause and never B's.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/spe-integration/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-fidelity-r4.5/notes/ws5-word-service-eval.md (Graph format=pdf behaviour: latency, 406 on protected files)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/spec.md (FR-16, FR-18, FR-40)</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="SpeFileStore delegation" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs">Virtual facade method delegating to an operations class.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read 130's projection DTO, 028's notes (ownership option chosen, setting names) and the sprk_documenttype choice values in dev; pick the existing value that fits a generated report (escalate if none).</step>
    <step order="1">Builder: title, firm, tracking number, outcome, billed and approved totals, findings table (subject, decision, reason, citation), totals reconciliation per I-1, generated-on date. Plain Fluent-neutral formatting; no images required.</step>
    <step order="2">SpeFileStore.DownloadAsPdfAsync(driveId, itemId) delegating to DriveItemOperations (Graph GET drive item content with format=pdf); map 406 and timeouts to SpaarkeStorageException with a stable code.</step>
    <step order="3">GenerateAsync: build docx → upload (SpeFileStore) → convert → upload PDF → delete docx → create sprk_document (app-only) → set sprk_reportdocument. Idempotency key on the outcome.</step>
    <step order="4">Route GET /api/v1/external/ebilling/{submissions|invoices}/{id}/report (directional), mounted with one line on the external group.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: every projection item (and nothing else) appears in the docx text; flag-off rule set clause absent; conversion failure leaves no document row and no link; second call reuses; route 401 / 403 other firm / 404 no report / 503 off / 200 PDF content type.</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build and dotnet test green; publish-size delta and vulnerable-package check recorded.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations (container choice, document type value, conversion latency seen in dev) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner wants the report in the core record's container instead of E-Billing Output Files (FR-40 says only "stored with the submission or invoice"), follow that; ask at Step 0 if 028's notes leave it open.</trigger>
    <trigger>If no existing sprk_documenttype value fits and a new option is needed, STOP: write it as an idempotent script under scripts/ebilling/ only after the main session agrees, and list it for 136 to sync into solution source.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Graph conversion is not available app-only on the output container (403 / 406 in dev), STOP and report; do not add a converter package or an out-of-process renderer.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SpeFileStore download / upload methods (no PDF conversion method exists — grep "format=pdf" in src finds none); DocumentFormat.OpenXml already referenced; spec section 11 has no row for the report service (FR-40 requirement).</existing>
    <extension>The conversion is one new method on the existing SpeFileStore facade (ADR-007), not a new service; the report builder is new because no generator renders eBilling outcomes.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No PDF report to attach to firm emails or download in the SPA (FR-40, D-36 fail; success criterion 6 fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/AdjustmentReportService.cs; Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs and DriveItemOperations.cs (one method); Api/Finance/AdjustmentReportEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/AdjustmentReportServiceTests.cs; tests/integration/contract/Api/AdjustmentReportEndpointsContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For a projection with N items, the generated document lists exactly those N items with their citations, and no other finding, internal note, confidence or document link.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The stored PDF is in the E-Billing Output Files container (or the owner-chosen container), linked by sprk_reportdocument, and the intermediate .docx no longer exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A conversion failure leaves no sprk_document row and no sprk_reportdocument link and returns a stable reason code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A second GenerateAsync for the same outcome creates no new document.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Download route: 401 unauthenticated, 403 for another firm's caller, 404 with a stable code when no report exists, 503 ebilling.disabled when off, 200 application/pdf for the own firm.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs and the external-group mount site in ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs (130 and 135 also add one line) — re-read before editing. SpeFileStore.cs is a hot shared facade: add one virtual method only and run /conflict-check before the PR. P5-B: no file overlap with 131, 134, 135.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
